A layered floating cake made of translucent crystalline slices, each layer revealing different glowing circuit patterns and data streams flowing between them, suspended in mid-air above an ornate Victorian dessert stand. The cake appears to be simultaneously whole and being consumed, with ethereal fork-shaped light beams taking bites that transform into streams of luminous particles. The scene is set in a moody, brass-accented steampunk laboratory with warm amber lighting from antique Edison-style fixtures, gears and pipes visible in the shadowy background. Rich burgundy and gold tones dominate, with electric blue data streams providing contrast. The crystalline cake layers show tiny reflected cityscapes and server room imagery within their faceted surfaces, suggesting multiple realities coexisting. Rendered in vintage Victorian illustration style with sepia undertones, crosshatching details, and aged paper texture, reminiscent of nineteenth-century scientific engravings with a fantastical twist.
